INSTRUCTIONS

For the instructions, <> will denote an input made by the user.
"" will denote an exact phrase that should be entered and otherwise, a parameter should be named



Orders must be placed by first calling the following input format:

	<"Order"> <Fascia model> <Car colour>
	
	

Only after 4 orders have been placed, can the user now call the Picker.
The User must input this sequence of events in order:

	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Ready">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 1">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 2">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 3">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 4">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 5">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 6">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 7">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"Pick 8">
	<"Picker"> <Picker name> <"To Marshalling">
	
If this sequence of order is not called in this precise order, the system will 
throw exceptions and not allow the user to do so
**********NOTE: the sequence of events must not be subsequent, but must be chronological



Only after at least one picker has been called <"To Marshalling"> may the user
call the sequencer. The user will input:

	<"Sequencer"> <Sequencer name> <"Sequences">
	


Only after there exists at least one order that has been sequenced may the Loader be called.
To call the Loader, the user will input:

	<"Loader"> <Loader name> <"Loads">
	


At any given time can the user call the replenisher to change supply in the warehouse.
To call the replenisher, the user must input:

	<"Replenisher"> <Replenisher name> <"Replenishes">
	
*********NOTE: regardless of the user not calling the replenisher, the system wil notify them when
inventory is low